lesson: 61
title: Counting on and counting back
stars: 0
explain: To count on, start at the number you have and say the next numbers, one for each step forward.
explain: To count back, say the numbers before it, one for each step back.
explain: From 34, counting on 3 gives 35, 36, 37; then counting back 2 gives 36, 35. The answer is 35.
vars: a=name n=10..80 k=2..6 j=2..5
need: k != j
answer: n + k - j
exercise: {a} is on step {n} of a long staircase. {a.He} climbs up {k} steps and then goes back down {j}. Which step is {a.he} on now?
exercise: {a} starts counting at {n}. {a.He} counts on {k} numbers and then counts back {j}. What number does {a.he} stop at?
exercise: A frog sits on stone number {n}. It hops forward {k} stones, then hops back {j} stones. On which stone number is the frog now?
exercise: {a} is on page {n} of a book. {a.He} flips ahead {k} pages, then flips back {j} pages. What page is {a.he} on?
exercise: The lift is on floor {n}. It goes up {k} floors and then down {j} floors. Which floor is it on now?
test: Counting back {j} from the number that comes {k} after {n}, where does {a} land?
test: After moving {k} squares ahead from square {n} and then {j} squares backward, which square is {a}'s counter on?
test: {a} has to say {k} numbers after {n} out loud and then step back {j}. Which number is {a.he} at in the end?
exercise: In a hotel in Toronto, {a} gets into the lift on floor {n}, rides up {k} floors, then rides down {j}. On which floor does {a.he} get out?
exercise: {a} is reading on a train to Dublin. {a.He} is on page {n}, reads on {k} pages, then turns back {j} pages to check something. Which page is {a.he} on?
exercise: Start at {n}. Count on {k}, then count back {j}. Where do you stop?
exercise: Which number do you reach if you count forward {k} from {n} and then backward {j}?
exercise: On a number line, {a} puts a finger on {n.words}, moves it {k.words} places to the right and then {j.words} places to the left. Which number is {a.his} finger on now?
exercise: A kangaroo in an Australian park stands by fence post number {n}. It bounds {k} posts further along, then hops back {j} posts. By which post is it now?
exercise: {a} is playing a board game in Wellington. {a.His} counter is on square {n}. {a.He} moves forward {k} squares, then has to go back {j} squares. Which square is the counter on now?
exercise: {a} sits in seat {n} in a long row at a cinema in London. {a.He} moves {k} seats along to the right, then {j} seats back to the left. In which seat is {a.he} now?
test: What number is {j} less than the number {k} more than {n}?
test: In a car park in Glasgow, {a} stops in bay {n}, then drives {k} bays forward and reverses {j} bays. Which bay is the car in?
test: Go up {k} from {n.words}, then down {j}. What number are you at?
test: {a}'s race number is {n}. {a.His} friend's number is {k} higher, and {a.his} cousin's number is {j} lower than the friend's. What is the cousin's number?
test: A snail in an Irish garden is at mark {n} on a measuring stick. It crawls up {k} marks and slides down {j}. At which mark does it stop?
test: Count back {j} after counting forward {k}, beginning at {n}. What is the final number?
exercise: ok so {a}'s on step {n+1} — no wait, step {n}. goes up {k}, back down {j}. what step now
exercise: frog on stone {n}, hops {k} forward then {j} back. which stone is it on lol
exercise: {a} on page {n}, flicks ahead {k}, oh and the book's got like 300 pages, then back {j}. what page is {a.he} on
exercise: Kai reckons start at {n}, count on {k}, back {j} gives {n+k+j}. nah thats wrong innit, whats the real number
