exam: Commencing at the integer {n}, a pupil is required to count forward by {k.words} consecutive integers and subsequently to count backward by {j.words}. State the integer at which the pupil terminates.
exam: It is given that a lift, initially stationary at floor {n}, ascends {k} floors and thereafter descends {j} floors. Determine the floor at which the lift is ultimately located.
exam: Ascertain the position of a counter which, having been placed upon square {n}, is advanced {k} squares and subsequently withdrawn {j} squares.
exam: Whereas {a} occupies step {n} of a staircase, and whereas {a.he} ascends {k} steps prior to descending {j}, identify the step hereinafter occupied by {a}.
exercise: {a} has {n} dollars in a money box. {a.His} nan, who passed away last spring, left {a.him} {k} dollars more, and {a.he} spends {j} on flowers for her grave. How many dollars does {a} have now?
exercise: The farm had {n} hens. {k} chicks hatched and grew up, then the fox got into the run and {j} hens went to the big henhouse in the sky. How many hens are on the farm now?
test: crap, {a} told porkies — said {a.he} got to step {n+k}, but really {a.he} climbed {k} from step {n} then slid back {j}. what step is {a.he} actually on
